# components.zd — user-defined components and modules (spec §14D).
#
# This file was written before the implementation existed, to test the
# design. Building the compiler against it found four things wrong with
# it, all listed at the bottom, and it is corrected here.

use "./model" for Item, visible

# A component is declared with `component` and used exactly like a
# built-in element. `Row` and `VoteCard` are indistinguishable at the
# call site — there is no privileged set of built-ins.
#
# `votes` is `durable`, so reading it in a client context yields
# `Remote of Whole`. The component does not launder that: it eliminates
# the variant with `when`, exactly as the view would have had to if this
# had been written inline. A component has no placement of its own.
component VoteCard with item, votes
    when votes
        Loading           show Spinner
        Failed with error show ErrorBar message is error.message
        Ready with tally
            Row item.name, padding is 8
                Text tally
                Button "vote"
                    on click
                        add 1 to votes

# Component-local state is scoped per instance, and must be `client`:
# a component instance is a browser-side thing, so `server` state
# (per-invocation) and `durable` state (shared) have no per-instance
# meaning. Two `Disclosure`s on one page open and close independently,
# because each instance declares its own `open`.
component Disclosure with label, children
    state open is client Truth starting no

    Column
        Button label
            on click
                set open to not open
        if open
            children

state votes     is durable Whole        starting 0
state catalogue is durable List of Item starting empty
state items     is server  List of Item from visible with catalogue

view
    Column
        Heading "Vote"

        when items
            Loading           show Spinner
            Failed with error show ErrorBar message is error.message
            Ready with list
                each item in list
                    # A component is colorless: it runs wherever its
                    # inputs are. `votes` is durable, so the obligation
                    # to handle Remote belongs to whoever reads it —
                    # passing it through a component cannot launder it.
                    VoteCard item, votes

        # Children nested at the call site are placed by the component
        # naming `children` in its body.
        Disclosure "Advanced"
            Row
                Text "nothing here yet"

# What writing the compiler against this file found wrong with §14D:
#
#   1. §14D.1's own `VoteCard` reads `votes at item.id` in the view, and
#      `votes` is `durable`. §5.2 makes that read `Remote of Map`, and
#      §14D.1's very next paragraph says a component receiving a remote
#      value must eliminate the variant. The example in the spec is the
#      laundering the spec says is impossible.
#   2. §14D.1's own `Disclosure` writes `if` in node position, which §4.4's
#      view grammar does not have. It is added here, with `ifInto` beside
#      `whenInto` in the runtime.
#   3. The first version of this file read `from allItems`, and nothing
#      declared `allItems`. A module is somewhere for it to live, which is
#      what `visible` is.
#   4. `votes` is one tally rather than a map, because `votes at item.id`
#      is `Option of Whole` and §14F.2a's `Option` elimination does not
#      exist yet. That is a prelude gap rather than a component one.
